        "comment_en": "Tyler Technologies' business model, characterized by high switching costs and a stable government client base, provides a solid foundation for sustaining superior Return on Invested Capital (ROIC) over the long term. While the provided ROE (10.7%) and ROA (5.6%) figures don't directly include WACC, the company consistently generates strong free cash flow (FCF TTM $714.3M), and its Piotroski F-Score of 7/9 indicates robust financial health. This stable cash flow and profitability suggest the company can consistently create value exceeding its cost of capital over the long run, demonstrating excellent capital allocation efficiency and resilience."
