        "comment_en": "Broadridge's services are deeply integrated with its financial institution clients' back-office systems and core operational processes, creating exceptionally high switching costs. These services are not merely technological solutions but rather the \"nervous system\" of clients' daily operations. Once a client chooses Broadridge, their data, processes, and employee training become deeply intertwined. Switching providers would entail not only significant financial expenditure but also potentially severe operational disruptions, data migration risks, and possible regulatory non-compliance. The complexity, high risk, and substantial cost associated with such a transition compel clients to maintain existing relationships, thereby building an impregnable moat for Broadridge."
