        "comment_en": "Broadridge processes an immense volume of transactions and investor communications across global financial markets, granting it unparalleled advantages in cost efficiency due to its sheer scale. Its substantial investments in technological infrastructure, data centers, and specialized personnel can be amortized over thousands of clients and millions of transactions, resulting in exceptionally low unit costs. New entrants aiming to achieve comparable service levels and cost-effectiveness would require astronomical capital outlays and face significant time and technological barriers. This economy of scale not only reduces Broadridge's operating costs but also enables it to offer more competitive pricing while maintaining high-profit margins, forming a crucial component of its robust moat."
