        "comment_en": "For the average consumer, the switching costs from a General Motors brand to another automaker are relatively low. While brand loyalty exists, the actual financial loss or operational inconvenience is not significant. Consumers can easily sell their old vehicle and purchase a new one without incurring high migration costs or system integration fees. This makes it difficult for GM to lock in customers through high switching costs, unlike certain software or financial services companies."
