        "comment_en": "The traditional automotive manufacturing business model typically lacks significant network effects. General Motors' large user base does not generate geometrically increasing value for existing users with each new addition. While an extensive dealer and service network offers convenience, this isn't the self-reinforcing network effect Buffett refers to. The accumulation of autonomous driving data might represent a nascent network effect, but it has not yet formed a decisive moat."
