        "comment_en": "JPMorgan Chase possesses an extensive physical network and deep local relationships across major global financial centers. This includes not only its worldwide offices but, more critically, its operating licenses under various national regulatory frameworks and long-established client trust. In certain highly specialized or capital-intensive financial service sectors, market capacity is limited, and entry barriers are extremely high, creating a natural oligopoly. New competitors would face immense capital, regulatory, and trust challenges, making it difficult to dislodge JPM's entrenched position."
