        "comment_en": "STERIS's business model primarily focuses on providing critical equipment and services to healthcare institutions, and its core value does not stem from direct user-to-user interaction. Consequently, it lacks typical \"two-sided network effects,\" where each additional user significantly enhances the product or service value for other users. While its widespread market penetration might lead to indirect effects like industry standardization or best practices, this fundamentally differs from the platform-based network effects emphasized by Buffett. Its competitive advantages are derived more from brand, patents, and switching costs, rather than network effects."
