        "comment_en": "Vertex consistently demonstrates exceptional financial performance, with a robust Return on Equity (ROE) of 21.8% and Return on Assets (ROA) of 16.1%, alongside a high Piotroski F-Score of 8/9. These metrics strongly indicate the company's ability to consistently generate returns significantly exceeding its Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC) over the long term. This not only proves the profitability and efficiency of its core business but also reflects its robust economic moat. Sustained excess ROIC is a key indicator Buffett uses to measure intrinsic value and moat strength, and Vertex excels in this regard."
