        "comment_en": "While Graco possesses proprietary designs and innovations in fluid handling technology and continuously invests in R&D, patent barriers in the industrial machinery sector are typically not as absolute as in pharmaceuticals or high-tech. Its moat is more rooted in accumulated technical expertise and manufacturing processes rather than singular patent monopolies. Although compliance with industry standards and regulations is a prerequisite for market entry, forming a certain barrier, it does not create an exclusive franchise. Thus, patents and regulations contribute to Graco's defensive advantages but are not its primary moat."
